        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f28819d3-4216-3d99-89ec-70e77ef501d2",
                "word": "dais",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79c0f8ee-d592-3c9e-ae84-ff766c70871b",
                        "entry_id": "f28819d3-4216-3d99-89ec-70e77ef501d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Table surélevée, estrade."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe4bc52d-98b6-4827-b516-18f9f7eab5a5",
                                "sense_id": "79c0f8ee-d592-3c9e-ae84-ff766c70871b",
                                "text": "La bonne femme s'assit sur les degrés du dais, aux pieds du jeune homme attentif et fixant sur elle un regard plein de bienveillance et de curiosité."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d4776ae5-c387-328c-998a-ecc99f9fde80",
                        "entry_id": "f28819d3-4216-3d99-89ec-70e77ef501d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ouvrage de bois, de tenture, etc., fait dans l’ancienne forme des ciels de lit et que l’on met en hauteur, au-dessus d’un maitre-autel, d’une chaire à prêcher, d’un trône, de la place où siègent, dans les occasions solennelles, certains personnages éminents, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4d1b691-57f9-4e14-bea4-9f22d503b94d",
                                "sense_id": "d4776ae5-c387-328c-998a-ecc99f9fde80",
                                "text": "On inaugurait le nouveau maire […] Nous, passâmes sous un dais tricolore ; le maire était avec toute sa famille sur un balcon ; nous le longeâmes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e9716fb-ad61-4aac-aaea-dfd4aaf92540",
                                "sense_id": "d4776ae5-c387-328c-998a-ecc99f9fde80",
                                "text": "Et là, le faisant asseoir sur une large stalle de chêne surmontée d’un dais de drap d’or, il prit place près de lui."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a520ce91-ac07-3338-bd62-19b2032ebce5",
                        "entry_id": "f28819d3-4216-3d99-89ec-70e77ef501d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Poêle soutenu de deux ou de quatre petits montants, sous lequel les prêtres catholiques portent le Saint-Sacrement, surtout dans les processions."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7f758df-ac1e-4647-92ec-4e38a13e9e79",
                                "sense_id": "a520ce91-ac07-3338-bd62-19b2032ebce5",
                                "text": "Marcher sous un dais."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39669f07-bd7c-40af-8872-0b4a361909d1",
                                "sense_id": "a520ce91-ac07-3338-bd62-19b2032ebce5",
                                "text": "Dans les rues, on eût dit un jour de procession, lorsque le passage du dais met les plus belles draperies aux fenêtres."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "00ad8bf5-077e-387a-8027-9041d701d6e6",
                        "entry_id": "f28819d3-4216-3d99-89ec-70e77ef501d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chose qui couvre : toit, ciel, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1684df03-a0cd-4a5c-abd8-af27f87f7bf0",
                                "sense_id": "00ad8bf5-077e-387a-8027-9041d701d6e6",
                                "text": "Amis reposons-nous sur ce siège sauvage,\nSous ce dais qu’ont formé la mousse et le feuillage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b7bc61c-c65e-4e8f-bcb1-472fa5d4cef4",
                                "sense_id": "00ad8bf5-077e-387a-8027-9041d701d6e6",
                                "text": "Les matinées de brouillard, un ciel d’une clarté faible, des nuées courant près de la terre sous un dais grisâtre convenaient aux phases de sa maladie morale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66e85547-ea35-4baf-8e10-08406c58f170",
                                "sense_id": "00ad8bf5-077e-387a-8027-9041d701d6e6",
                                "text": "Mais soudain, au bord occidental de l’immense dais noir, le soleil couchant reparaît un instant, sanglant, embrasant le camp entier d’une lueur surnaturelle. Les tentes semblent flamber, toutes rouges entre la plaine d’un vert invraisemblable et les nuages violacés […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b1b3047-b57f-497f-82e1-c959db005301",
                                "sense_id": "00ad8bf5-077e-387a-8027-9041d701d6e6",
                                "text": "Mes grands-parents des Pyrénées mangeaient à la cuisine comme des laboureurs de Le Nain. Cuisine de paysans, cuisine de princes. Dans sa cheminée on aurait pu faire rôtir un bœuf. À son plafond, pendait un dais royal : les épis de maïs et le jambon."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "61472047-903d-39ec-9504-d6629fae3e70",
                        "entry_id": "f28819d3-4216-3d99-89ec-70e77ef501d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Toit démontable que l’on met sur les voitures découvertes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b9d931e-77fa-41f6-913a-1c8217ace8a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "f28819d3-4216-3d99-89ec-70e77ef501d2",
                        "source_sense_description": "Table surélevée, estrade",
                        "target_lang_word": "dais",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dais",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a9e4736e-453b-32f0-99a4-907e490b73c8",
                                        "entry_id": "55d04a9b-51e8-35c9-92f9-f503fa8a82d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A raised platform in a room for a high table, a seat of honour, a throne, or other dignified occupancy, such as ancestral statues; a similar platform supporting a lectern, pulpit, etc., which may be used to speak from."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd87c948-c49c-4205-9cc3-01fee41ea360",
                                                "sense_id": "a9e4736e-453b-32f0-99a4-907e490b73c8",
                                                "text": "Many of the figures, clad in mail from head to foot, were ranged above the dais; and she could almost fancy a skeleton form beneath, or that wild and fearful eyes glared through the apertures of the closed visors."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03ade28c-d06b-4924-9a88-5113e03daf8d",
                                                "sense_id": "a9e4736e-453b-32f0-99a4-907e490b73c8",
                                                "text": "At last we came to the head of the cave, where there was a rock daïs almost exactly similar to the one on which we had been so furiously attacked, a fact that proved to me that these daïs must have been used as altars, probably for the celebration of religious ceremonies, and more especially of rites connected with the interment of the dead. On either side of this daïs were passages leading, Billali informed me, to other caves full of dead bodies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "061f2460-2c64-4fdc-90f9-7b59b8c2bf4f",
                                                "sense_id": "a9e4736e-453b-32f0-99a4-907e490b73c8",
                                                "text": "Babbitt's party politely edged through them and into the whitewashed room, at the front of which was a dais with a red-plush throne and a pine altar painted watery blue, as used nightly by the Grand Masters and Supreme Potentates of innumerable lodges."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db71003d-ebd9-467a-a13e-27c3b21a41e6",
                                                "sense_id": "a9e4736e-453b-32f0-99a4-907e490b73c8",
                                                "text": "A dais wife is a woman who sits at a round table with the wives of other men who are seated on the dais. Her husband sits on the dais, raised above the other people in the room, including his wife."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49605625-a44e-4610-bb06-8af2c78251cc",
                                                "sense_id": "a9e4736e-453b-32f0-99a4-907e490b73c8",
                                                "text": "The daises of the Northwest Colonnade and the South Temple of the Warriors, the Mercado benches, and the benches of the Southeast Patio of the Iglesia are other instances where large groups of individuals in processions are shown."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e3da0e4-34f6-4cae-8f2e-e49c27f02e8e",
                                                "sense_id": "a9e4736e-453b-32f0-99a4-907e490b73c8",
                                                "text": "“We gathered all the people that love you into this one room. And then when we saw all the empty chairs, we decided to drag some randos in off the street to fill them!” [drum plays rim shot] [laughter] “So many illustrious guests here on the dais tonight. And also Colin Robinson.” [rim shot] [laughter] “He got me, I got got.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00f07f00-15fb-3405-8f4e-834e51d7674a",
                                        "entry_id": "55d04a9b-51e8-35c9-92f9-f503fa8a82d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bench, a settle, a pew."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "Northern",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79d5214e-1ad9-4b69-80a1-4c0785d56fe1",
                                                "sense_id": "00f07f00-15fb-3405-8f4e-834e51d7674a",
                                                "text": "[page 211] The Mer-man he stept o'er ae deas, / And he has steppit over three: / \"O maiden, pledge me faith and troth! / O Marstig's daughter, gang wi' me!\" […] [pages 213–214] Notes on The Mer-man. […] I remember having seen in the hall of the ruined castle of Elan Stalker, in the district of Appin, an old oaken deas, which was so contrived as to serve for a sittee; at meal-times the back was turned over, rested upon the arms, and became a table; and at night the seat was raised up, and displayed a commodious bed for four persons, two and two, feet to feet, to sleep in. I was told, that this kind of deas was formerly common in the halls of great houses, where such œconomy, with respect to bed-room, was very necessary."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "794f71b0-696c-496d-bd86-74841f718f6a",
                                                "sense_id": "00f07f00-15fb-3405-8f4e-834e51d7674a",
                                                "text": "DAIS, Dess, Deas […] A long board, seat or bench erected against a wall. […] A pew in a church"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2932a5e-1842-386b-ac08-d9cc674b837f",
                                        "entry_id": "55d04a9b-51e8-35c9-92f9-f503fa8a82d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An elevated table in a hall at which important people were seated; a high table."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "012287d5-9542-4cd7-a8c5-9d4a8effa663",
                                                "sense_id": "a2932a5e-1842-386b-ac08-d9cc674b837f",
                                                "text": "As the principal table was always placed upon a dais, it began very soon, by a natural abuse of words, to be called itself a Dais, and people were said to sit at the dais, instead of at the table upon the dais."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e61d719-5e14-386a-923d-e3b4e0f05cac",
                                        "entry_id": "55d04a9b-51e8-35c9-92f9-f503fa8a82d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The canopy over an altar, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
